+---
+id: task-001-spring-campaign-discount-codes
+type: task
+title: "Spring campaign discount codes"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Spring campaign discount codes
+
+For the spring newsletter, customers get discount codes. An order takes one code at most; a second code replaces the
+first.
+
+## Codes
+
+- `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € (500 cents) off the order's items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € (3000 cents)
+  or more.
+- An unknown code is refused with an error that says so. `WELCOME5` on a smaller order is refused with an error that
+  says why. A refused code leaves the order as it was.
+- The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before any discount.
+
+## Interface
+
+- `applyCode(orderNumber, code)` on the order book: applies a code to the order with that number.
+- An order's totals show `discountCents` (0 without a code), and `totalCents` is items minus discount plus shipping.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Each code is tested for its happy path and for its error path (unknown code, `WELCOME5` below 30.00 €).
+- Rounding of `SPRING10` is tested at the half-cent boundary.
+- A second code replaces the first; a refused code leaves the earlier code in place.
+- Shipping is charged or waived on the items before discount, and not reduced by the discount.
+- The changelog records the change and the package version is bumped to match.
